  "name": "Compound nouns",
  "level": "A2",
  "status": "geprueft",
  "subtitle": "A compound noun is two nouns that work as one: bus + stop = bus stop. The second noun is the main one: a bus stop is a stop, not a bus. The first noun is usually singular: a shoe shop.",
  "briefMarks": [
    "compound noun",
    "second noun",
    "singular"
  ],
  "source": "EnglishAcademy original English text (grammar-a2 run, 2026-10-29)",
  "concept": {
