    "exampleHtml": "a <span class=\"vp-prep\">bus</span> <span class=\"vp-verb\">stop</span> · a <span class=\"vp-prep\">tooth</span><span class=\"vp-verb\">brush</span> · a <span class=\"vp-prep\">shoe</span> <span class=\"vp-verb\">shop</span>",
    "qa": [
      {
        "html": "Two nouns can make a <strong>new noun</strong>: <em>bus + stop = bus stop</em>. We use them all the time: <em>bedroom, toothbrush, train station, football match</em>.",
        "tag": "Noun + noun"
      },
      {
        "html": "The <strong>second noun</strong> is the main one. The first noun says what kind or what for. <em>A bus stop is a stop. A toothbrush is a brush. A train station is a station.</em> Not <s>a stop bus</s>.",
        "tag": "The second noun"
      },
      {
        "html": "The <strong>first noun</strong> is usually <strong>singular</strong>, even if the meaning is plural: <em>a shoe shop</em> (a shop for shoes), <em>a car park</em>, <em>a ten-minute walk</em>, <em>a two-hour film</em>. A few are different: <em>a clothes shop, a sports centre</em>.",
        "tag": "First noun: singular"
      },
      {
        "html": "For the <strong>plural</strong>, change the second noun: <em>two bus stops, three toothbrushes, four bedrooms</em>.",
        "tag": "Plural"
      },
      {
        "html": "Compounds are written <strong>as one word</strong> (<em>bedroom, toothbrush</em>), <strong>as two words</strong> (<em>bus stop, train station</em>) or <strong>with a hyphen</strong> (<em>a ten-minute walk</em>). There is no simple rule: check a dictionary and learn the common ones as whole words.",
        "tag": "Spelling"
      },
      {
        "html": "The <strong>stress</strong> is usually on the <strong>first part</strong>: <em>BUS stop, TOOTHbrush, BEDroom, CAR park</em>.",
        "tag": "Stress"
      },
      {
        "html": "Typical mistakes: ✗ <em>a shoes shop</em> → ✓ <em>a shoe shop</em> · ✗ <em>a stop bus</em> → ✓ <em>a bus stop</em> · ✗ <em>a ten-minutes walk</em> → ✓ <em>a ten-minute walk</em>",
        "tag": "Typical mistakes"
      }
    ],
    "noteHtml": "Some compounds have an <em>-ing</em> word or an adjective as the first part: <em>swimming pool, washing machine, greenhouse</em>. Learn these as whole words. For the plural of the second noun, see <a href=\"/plurals\">Plurals</a>. For nouns in general, see <a href=\"/nouns\">Nouns</a>.",
